#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
# pc-panel: a local web dashboard to monitor and control a Linux PC.
# It measures RAM, graphics card, processor, network, disks, system health and what
# is running, and shows it on a local page:   http://127.0.0.1:47822
# It only reads the system. What it writes: its own settings (~/.config/pc-panel),
# the black box, 24 h history and SSD error counts (~/.local/state/pc-panel), game
# sessions (~/.local/share/pc-panel/sessoes.jsonl), the CSV log when enabled in Settings,
# the tray files in $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/pc-panel, and the fan command file
# (/var/lib/pc-panel/fans.json, applied by the root helper pc-panel-fans).
# With the page closed and nothing asking for samples (logging, graphics card
# curve, fixed fan speed) the service sleeps and costs nothing.
# The tray icon (pc-panel-tray) starts and stops this service and sets the port.
# MIT license. Identifiers are still in Portuguese; the interface has English and Portuguese.
import bisect
